  "description": {
    "text": "Battle Road Spring 2005 held nine tournaments in seven cities from 13 March 2005, open to players who had applied in advance; the Kyushu tournament, called off on 20 March by an earthquake, was finished on 8 May. Everyone in the qualifying round got Ryo Ueda's Celebi ex, finalists a holo Dark Metal Energy, and the top three of each age division the Victory Ring, redrawn that year with Pikachu, in an acrylic plaque. The junior and senior winners went to the 2005 World Championships in the United States.",
